# NDT4 Accessibility

Follow [Foundation / Accessibility](https://webtheme.nd.edu/?path=/docs/foundation-accessibility--docs) and WCAG 2.0/2.1 AA for contrast.

## Visual

- Do not convey meaning with color alone; underline links and use distinct colors.
- Provide meaningful `alt` text for images (empty alt only for decorative images).
- Use logical heading order (`h1` → `h2` → …); do not skip levels for styling.
- Link text must provide context — never “click here” or bare “read more”.

## Contrast and type

- Normal text: contrast ≥ 4.5:1; large text (≥24px or ≥18.66px bold): ≥ 3:1.
- Do not override NDT default font colors.
- Prefer left-aligned body copy; centered text hurts readability.

## Interaction and media

- Interactive controls need adequate target size for mobility impairments.
- Support keyboard navigation; do not rely on mouse-only affordances.
- Videos need captions when audio carries meaning.
- Prefer plain language over jargon when possible.

## Motion

- Wrap custom animation CSS in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.
- Prefer NDT `.animate` / `.animate--*` classes from `animate.css` when motion is needed.
